n ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["GeneDx Holdings Corp. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.9B market cap on $428M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +51.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -69% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","The business throws off $14M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -10.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 7.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 266% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.657547962836918},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (38.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmi